------------------------

The RGPL's closing section suggests putting a short notice at the top of every
source file, so a file that gets copied out of here still says what it is. That
is a suggestion, not an obligation -- a license file at the root is enough to
license the work, and nothing in this repository is out of compliance for
lacking headers. The only thing skipping them costs is that a lone file, torn
out of context and mailed to somebody, arrives carrying no evidence of its own
terms.

